# Shared Packages

Source of truth: `docs/architecture/shared-packages.md`.

## Allowed Shared Libs

| Package | Contents |
|---------|----------|
| `shared-kernel-types` (`packages/shared/kernel-types`) | Branded IDs (`UserId`, `TenantId`, …), cross-cutting enums |
| `contracts` (`packages/shared/contracts`) | Zod API schemas, `HttpStatus`, error/pagination envelopes |
| `utils` (`packages/shared/utils`) | Pure helpers (`ObjectUtils`, `ArrayUtils`, `DateUtils`, …) |
| `config` (`packages/shared/config`) | `ConfigLoader` (YAML + Zod; pluggable `source`) |

**Utils consumption / extension:** always import from `@b2b-saas-starter-kit/utils`. When a generic helper is missing, extend `packages/shared/utils` (class + tests + barrel) — do not fork local helpers. See `general/utils.mdc`.

**Config:** always load via `ConfigLoader` from `@b2b-saas-starter-kit/config`. Apps own schemas and value files. See `general/config.mdc`.

No `constants` package. Domain base classes (`AggregateRoot`, `DomainEvent`) stay in `domain/shared-kernel` (backend-only).

## DAG

```
shared-kernel-types  ← leaf
contracts            → shared-kernel-types
domain               → shared-kernel-types   (NOT contracts)
frontend / api       → contracts + shared-kernel-types
config               → utils (+ Zod)
```

```typescript
// ✅
import type { TenantId } from '@b2b-saas-starter-kit/shared-kernel-types'
import { InviteMemberInputSchema } from '@b2b-saas-starter-kit/contracts'
import { ConfigLoader } from '@b2b-saas-starter-kit/config'

// ❌ domain must never import contracts
import { InviteMemberInput } from '@b2b-saas-starter-kit/contracts'
```

## Must Never Be Shared

- Domain / business rules
- TypeORM, Redis, Nest, React
- Context-internal types that are not wire contracts
- Side effects at import time

When unsure: keep it context-local rather than dumping into `utils` / `config`.
